{"Title":"An Act relative to minimizing suffering during the commitment process","BillNumber":"S1041","DocketNumber":"SD1661","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JBL0","Name":"Joan B. Lovely","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBL0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T08:52:44.623"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JBL0","Name":"Joan B. Lovely","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBL0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T08:52:44.6233333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1041/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Lovely, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1041) of Joan B. Lovely for legislation relative to minimizing suffering during the commitment process.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSection 35 of chapter 123 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking, in lines 43-45 the words:- \"The court shall order examination by a qualified physician, a qualified psychologist or a qualified social worker”, and inserting in place thereof the following:-\r\n\tUpon appearance or apprehension, the court shall have the individual examined by a physician or a qualified advanced practice registered nurse designated to have the authority to admit to a facility. If the physician or qualified advanced registered nurse reports that the failure to hospitalize or provide medical treatment to the individual would create a likelihood of serious harm, the court shall order the individual with alcohol or substance use disorder to be committed to a facility designated by the department of public health for treatment during the pendency of the petition.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}